The latest MSTest is **4.2.3**. Here are the breaking changes affecting your code:

## 1. `[ExpectedException]` removed (compile error)

The attribute no longer exists in MSTest 4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

## 2. `Assert.ThrowsException` removed

If you were considering that as a stepping stone — it's also gone in v4. Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` (exact type match) or `Assert.Throws` (allows derived types).

## 3. MSTEST0032 warning (severity escalated)

`Assert.IsTrue(true)` triggers a "review always-true condition" warning (now `Warning` severity in 4.x, was `Info`).

---

### To upgrade

Update `TestProject.csproj`:
```xml
<PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="4.2.3" />
```

Then fix both `[ExpectedException]` usages. Would you like me to apply these changes?
